  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(y+3)^{2}=9(x-2)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y+3)^{2}=4(\\frac{9}{4})(x-2).\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{9}{4}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=2$ and $k=-3.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(2,-3).$",
